### 1.3 Randomized Interior Layout System (Module Assembly Pipeline)

Interiors are assembled from authored room modules by a three-pass pipeline, so no two structures share a layout while every layout stays navigable, fair and performant.

**Pass A — Mission Graph (topology).** Each structure type owns a graph grammar: `Start → Entrance · Hub{2–4} · Branch{1–3} · Vault`. Rewrite rules expand nodes into rooms, then the generator inserts Locks (locked door, power gate, valve, vine block, collapsed passage) and their Keys. Invariants:

- **Key-before-Lock:** every Key node is reachable without passing its Lock.
- **Loop-backs:** insert 1–2 shortcut edges (one-way drop, ladder, lift) so routes form circuits.
- **Depth:** the Vault sits at ≥ 60% of max graph depth.
- **Pacing:** at most 3 consecutive dead-end nodes; every 4th node is a decision point (≥ 2 exits).

| Structure | Graph nodes | Mandatory nodes | Gate types |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Hydro-Dam | 14–22 | Crest Entrance, Control Room, Sluice Gallery, Turbine Hall | Power, Valve, Lift |
| Rail Yard | 12–20 | Gatehouse, Switch Tower, Roundhouse, Strongbox Car | Switch, Vine, Turntable |
| Mountain Tunnel | 10–16 | Portal, Signal Box, Plug, Powder Magazine | Debris, Gas, Shaft |
| Automated Factory | 18–30 | Loading Dock, Assembly Spine, 4 Power Sectors, Vault | Breaker, Lockdown, Code fragments |

**Pass B — Module Fit (geometry).** Modules are authored on a 4 × 4 × 3.2 m grid (S = 1×1, M = 2×2, L = 3×4, XL = 4×4 or double height) and expose typed Sockets:

```
module: dam_gallery_L_03
size: [3, 1, 4]            # grid cells
role: [Corridor, Junction]
theme: [Dam]
sockets:
  - {id: N0, type: DOOR_STD,   pos: [0, 0, 2],  dir: N,  width: 1}
  - {id: S0, type: DOOR_BLAST, pos: [2, 0, -2], dir: S,  width: 2}
  - {id: U0, type: LADDER,     pos: [1, 1, 0],  dir: UP, width: 1}
variants: {damage: [intact, damaged, collapsed], mirror: true}
slots: {container: 2, clutter: 8, hazard: 1, lore: 1, light: 3}
navmesh: baked_local_tiles    # stitched at socket pairs
```

The solver is a constraint-propagation pass (WFC-style entropy ordering) over mission-graph nodes. Candidates are filtered by role, size, theme, socket compatibility and the occupancy grid; contradictions backtrack up to 64 steps, then reseed (`attempt` is part of `InteriorSeed`, max 8 attempts). The final fallback is a hand-authored Gold Layout, so generation can never fail.

| Variation lever | Options | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Module choice | 4–9 candidates per role | About 5^12 ≈ 2.4 × 10^8 topologies per structure |
| Transform | 4 rotations; mirror if flagged symmetric-safe | Breaks memorized silhouettes |
| Damage state | Intact / Damaged / Collapsed (Decay Noise map) | Collapsed variants seal sockets and force alternate routes |
| Environment modifier | Flooded, Overgrown, Dark, Frozen, Sparking | Material swaps, hazards, NavMesh cost changes |
| Dressing set | 3–5 per theme | Changes props, color, lore |

**Pass C — Dressing and validation.** Slots are filled by theme: Container, Clutter, Hazard, Lore, Light, Entity. Rules: adjacent rooms never share a dressing set; 1 lore beat per 3 rooms; container density by room role (Storage 4–8, Office 1–3, Corridor 0–1). Validation gates:

1. BFS reachability from Entrance to every Key, Lock and Vault.
2. NavMesh stitch with OffMeshLinks at doors, ladders, stairs and vents (no runtime bake, under 4 ms per structure).
3. Corridor sightlines capped at 28 m without a decision point.
4. At most 12 shadow-casting dynamic lights per module.
5. Portal-based occlusion: every module is a cell, every door a portal.

**Streaming and network.** The graph and solver are pure data jobs on a worker thread. Output is an `InteriorBlueprint` (list of `moduleId, transform, variantFlags, dressingSeed`; a few KB). Instantiation is time-sliced (≤ 2 ms per frame): shell plus first 3 modules at 250 m, remaining modules on door proximity. Interiors are never replicated: the server sends `(StructureSeed, attempt)`, and each client regenerates and verifies a CRC32 `LayoutHash`; a mismatch triggers a blueprint resync. Anti-repetition: a ring buffer of the last 12 interiors rejects any candidate whose module-set Jaccard similarity to a recent same-type interior exceeds 0.6. Interiors use probe-based GI baked per module prefab plus dynamic local lights.

