## 4. Advanced Multiplayer Roles & Loop

### 4.1 Netcode Topology & Crew Presence

Modes: **Host/Client** (listen server; the host is authoritative) and **Dedicated** (headless). The simulation is server-authoritative; clients predict their own movement.

| Entity | Rate | Method | Authority |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Player (grounded on train) | 30 Hz inputs, 20 Hz snapshots | Replicated in train-local coordinates plus `FrameId`; client prediction and reconciliation | Server |
| Train | 20 Hz | 1D spline state (`s`, speed, brake pressure) as doubles; cars derive from `s` | Server |
| Levers and valves | Event, plus 20 Hz while held | Value with Authority Lock | Server; the grabber owns the lock |
| Coal chunks and loose props | 15 Hz within 6 m of a player; asleep otherwise | Server physics, interpolated on clients | Server |
| Forgotten and the Pursuit entity | 10 Hz (5 Hz beyond 80 m) | Snapshot interpolation; Pursuit entity as a spline position | Server |
| Containers, doors, structures | Event-driven | Seed plus delta flags | Server |
| Atmosphere | On join plus drift correction | `t`, timescale, night count | Server |

Lag compensation for hitscan and melee uses a 200 ms rewind buffer. Streaming uses the union of per-player Interest Spheres (structures 1.5 km, terrain 800 m).

**Crew Presence Lock.** The throttle locks at 0 while any crew member is more than 300 m from the train (flagged Away) or Left Behind, unless the Engineer holds the lever for 3 s with a horn warning (Departure Override). This prevents a Scavenger from being abandoned by accident while keeping the departure a conscious, social decision.

### 4.2 Roles and Division of Labor

Roles are soft classes: anyone can do anything, but specialists are faster, safer and see more. Role Cards are picked at session start and swapped at any Station Roster Terminal.

