### 4.5 Persistence: Biome Station Saves vs. Mid-Track Disconnects

**Save architecture.** Two layers: a **Station Commit** (the permanent save) and a **Transit Journal** (crash and disconnect protection). Both use versioned schemas, zstd compression and atomic writes (write temp, fsync, rename). Three rolling backups of each Station Commit are kept.

| Data | Station Commit | Transit Journal |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Train block layout, car contents | Yes | Yes |
| Train dynamic state (spline `s`, speed, boiler, fuel) | Reset to Station siding | Yes |
| Player inventories, stats, roles (Crew Manifest) | Yes | Yes |
| Containers, structure deltas (looted, cleared, repaired) | Yes | Yes (delta log) |
| Time of day, night count, Pursuit schedule | Yes | Yes |
| Live Pursuit state | Not applicable (never at a Station) | Phase checkpoints every 60 s |
| Mob positions, thrown or dropped transients | Never | Never |

**Biome Station commit flow.** Stations sit at biome boundaries and host the Save Ledger, Fuel Depot, Customization Bay (heavy block placement), Roster Terminal, Storage Lockers and Infirmary. Interacting with the Ledger (any crew member; the others get a confirm prompt) freezes simulation for 1–2 s, serializes the full world delta in a background job, writes atomically, then confirms. The commit is the only permanent rollback point. Docking inside the 150 m sanctuary also pauses Forgotten spawning. Departure through the Biome Gate generates the next biome from the saved seed.

**Mid-track disconnect resolution** (the world keeps running while at least one player remains):

| Player situation at disconnect | Server action | On rejoin |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Inside the train or perimeter | Avatar becomes a Dormant Body (invulnerable, non-colliding), then moves to the nearest bunk after 30 s | Wakes in the bunk, inventory intact |
| Outside, daytime | Invulnerable and frozen for 120 s, then teleported to the nearest bunk if the train is stationary, otherwise marked Stranded | Spawns at the last bunk; items left outside stay as a drop pile |
| Outside at night, or inside a structure | Safeguard: 120 s invulnerability and a 5 m Field Beacon bubble around the avatar | As above |
| Downed or during a Pursuit | Bleed-out timer pauses; revive priority flagged to the Medic | Revive state resumes |
| Mid-clamber or mid-jump | Resolve physics, snap to the last stable surface | As above |
| Carrying a shared heavy item | Item drops on a stable surface | Item recoverable |

The slot is reserved for 10 minutes (configurable). After that, the player’s Crew Manifest entry (inventory, role, stats, bunk assignment) persists in the world and they can rejoin any time at their bunk. Late joiners spawn in a bunk with 20 s invulnerability, even mid-Pursuit.

**Host or whole-server loss.**

- **Dedicated server, last player leaves:** Hibernation. The Dead-Man’s Brake stops the train within 60 s, world time freezes, and no fuel or emitter ticks accrue. There is no offline progress and no offline attack.
- **Listen-server host quits or crashes:** the session ends for clients. The host machine writes an Emergency Transit Save (journal plus last snapshot). The next load resumes from it as a one-use Suspend Slot, consumed on load and replaced by the next Station Commit, which prevents save-scumming.
- **Resume rules:** the train resumes at its last stable position with the Dead-Man’s Brake applied. A Pursuit resumes from its last phase checkpoint with Gap −150 m. Irreversible events (car shear, item loss, death) are appended to a write-ahead journal and fsynced before they resolve, so quitting cannot undo them.

|  | Mid-track disconnect | Biome Station save |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Trigger | Network drop, quit, crash | Ledger interaction |
| Scope | Player avatar plus journal; world continues | Entire world delta, atomic |
| Rollback point | No (Suspend Slot is consumed on load) | Yes, 3 rolling backups |
| World state | Continues (1+ players) or hibernates (0) | Station layover; spawns paused; a pending Pursuit is deferred |

